{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern","id":501754,"title":"Second Edition concept concern","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-03T09:20:31-07:00","id":501754,"title":"Second Edition concept concern","content":"Is there going to be any provision for what I consider a classic motif: the man (or woman) who makes a bargain, serves for a time in Arcadia, then goes back to Earth because the agreed-upon term is over? Let's suppose you've got a woman who's very ugly, and desperately wants to be beautiful. &quot;Serve me for ten years and I will make you beautiful,&quot; says a True Fae, and the woman agrees. Ten years come and go, during which time she does scutwork in the Keeper's territory, gets subjected to horribly painful beauty treatments, gets ordered into her Keeper's bed now and then, and when her term is up, she gets returned to Earth, as a <i>knockout.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:25:53-07:00","id":501776,"title":"","content":"Seeing as its been mentioned several times in the spoiled stuff that some people choose to go to a Keeper? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:43:56-07:00","id":501808,"title":"","content":"Sure. Sounds like a character with No Seeming, which has more or less been confirmed to be a thing in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:20:56-07:00","id":501865,"title":"","content":"If the Keeper releases then they just come out Seemingless usually (some exceptions perhaps, such as a Fairest who sneaks other changelings out with her).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:03:21-07:00","id":502544,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering on other ways a Keeper may deliberately let the changeling go... One comes to mind of a changeling made to be a kind of escort for the Keeper at wondrous balls and the changeling actively commits as many faux pas and breaks taboos to be 'fired'... Effectively being let go and becoming a Beast along with it.<br /> <br /> Darklings could stomp down all others when a Keeper offers a 'prize' of being sent back to reality to all it's subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T04:57:20-07:00","id":502777,"title":"","content":"I'd say they're Seemingless, and no &quot;true&quot; Lost would trust them in the slightest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T05:01:42-07:00","id":502783,"title":"","content":"Why not? Fae are capricious bastards and throw their old toys away all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:21:35-07:00","id":502880,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I can think of quite a few scenarios where a changeling could depart without getting a Seeming. The completed contract,t for example, doesn't require the reclaiming of self-determination because it doesn't involve the loss of self-determination in the first place.Strike a deal, fulfill the deal, go home. Or a Keeper gets an enthusiasm for superheroes, and drafts a bunch of superheroes (and super villains). Then he gets interested in Regency romance and goes out and drafts a bunch of romance novel characters, forgetting about eh superheroes, who are now able to wander off, and do. The Fae are the exemplars of being mercurial.Or one of them find that the palace or zoo is getting overcrowded. Time to clear out old stock. You could even have a Fae that exists as something like a tropical island, and keeps itself occupied by arranging for people to wreck or otherwise be marooned on itself, and then complicating their lives. At some point, the shipwreck victims will usually get off the island, and the Gentry will get some new ones. That's just how it works. Some Gentry don't want to keep people for long periods; they've designed themselves for constant turnover, like the Happy Island Fun Fair I once dreamed up. It's not sure why it needs an exit, but it does, and so it has one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:39:27-07:00","id":503263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=502783#post502783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Fae are capricious bastards and throw their old toys away all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced that a lot of changelings would buy that. &quot;I had to chew a leg off to escape my Keeper and yours just let you go? Pull the other one, it's prosthetic, <i>loyalist</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:51:02-07:00","id":503412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=502777#post502777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say they're Seemingless, and no &quot;true&quot; Lost would trust them in the slightest</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=503263#post503263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced that a lot of changelings would buy that. &quot;I had to chew a leg off to escape my Keeper and yours just let you go? Pull the other one, it's prosthetic, <i>loyalist</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Coupla counter-points:<br /> 1) You're assuming that it's really obvious when a character has a Seeming. Direct from the developer, this is not the case (see quote below).<br /> 2) We don't actually know the demographic makeup of Seemings/Seeming-less in a &quot;general&quot; Changeling population (for whatever sense that makes). If the majority of Changelings have no Seeming, and those who do are exceptions, then this would be a weird standard to develop.<br /> 3) Speaking with Changelings from other Keepers and comparing notes would make the sheer diversity abundantly plain really, really quickly. The full span of what they will or won't do is going to come across as obviously broad and generally kind of insane. &quot;I wouldn't put anything past them,&quot; seems like it'd be a pretty common sentiment. Some of the Gentry just letting their Changelings go is hardly inconceivable, particularly if a bargain was involved, as that's likely one of the few points of consistency Changelings will come across. There's not much stopping some of those who clawed their ways out from looking down on or resenting those who didn't, but I don't anticipate outright disbelief to be so common. Particularly since I imagine decking everyone out in pledges and oaths is relatively standard operating procedure anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498214#post498214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming, at least in the perception I currently have, is a much less concrete thing. Depending on your Kith, you could probably pass for a given Seeming without one. You might be a lacklustre example, but an example none the less. For example, if you're a Seeming-free Draconic, you might pretend to be a Beast with just some heavy behavior acting.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:15:38-07:00","id":503539,"title":"","content":"I honestly think that concept works in either edition.<br /> <br /> It does sound more to me like a Fairest than No Seeming, but that would be up to the player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:22:43-07:00","id":503545,"title":"","content":"I have this weird prediction that someone who &quot;serves their time&quot; will be Elemental. Completely baseless, mind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:12:11-07:00","id":503592,"title":"","content":"Aren't there several fairy tales that are based around agreeing to a period of servitude? So yeah, I can see this being a possibility. As for them being Seemingless, that could vary on the situation.<br /> <br /> All the Seeming is, is you establishing your own power and independence. So the way I see it, the Changeling could still develop a Seeming based on how they decide to use their new &quot;gifts&quot; once they've been released. Loyalists don't have a Seeming because, well, they're still submissive to their Keeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Did the woman want to become beautiful so she could get invited to the hotest parties and have sex with all the cute guys? She's a beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did she want to become beautiful in order to get people to pay attention to her and do what she asks of them? She's a fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did she want to become beautiful to spite an X-lover or make a family member jealous? She's a Darkling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-04-2015, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:47:03-07:00","id":503619,"title":"","content":"I can the No-Seeming as looked down on by the others (ala Nosferatu in Vampire), perhaps they need to go through some type of task to prove their disdain of the Gentry when they come to the local Freehold, to show they're not a Privateer, though once cleared they're likely just as welcome as any other changeling and have their own part in the Freehold meetings and day-to-day goings on. But also it's been said that a No-Seeming may walk amongst other changelings and never have their lack of it come up.<br /> It seems that due to the mass of kith and how a Seeming can change it to be something else, it is likely much harder in 2e to group changeling's Seemings up by appearance only like it was in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:08:34-07:00","id":505134,"title":"","content":"For those who are simply abandoned, doesn't a Changeling needs a little bit more than freedom from direct capture to actually get back from Arcadia to the normal world? There are a couple of descriptors of Fae realms that at least suggest as such. So wouldn't a seeming be not just about getting away from the Fea master, but also Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:33:20-07:00","id":505161,"title":"","content":"I really don't understand why the &quot;no seeming&quot; thing even exists as the inevitable result of being willingly let go by the fae. Can someone explain why that's a worthwhile change to the game, or why it's worth subtracting the mechanical advantage/interest of seemings from that plethora of interesting character backstories?<br /> <br /> I know I can come across as overly negative at times - but I'm this one has me scratching my head more than most... and I'm not generally familiar enough with Changeling as it stands to hold an opinion other than my first impression of &quot;this feels like punishing players for choosing to pursue some interesting story points.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T02:01:01-07:00","id":505166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=505161#post505161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand why the &quot;no seeming&quot; thing even exists as the inevitable result of being willingly let go by the fae. Can someone explain why that's a worthwhile change to the game, or why it's worth subtracting the mechanical advantage/interest of seemings from that plethora of interesting character backstories?<br /> <br /> I know I can come across as overly negative at times - but I'm this one has me scratching my head more than most... and I'm not generally familiar enough with Changeling as it stands to hold an opinion other than my first impression of &quot;this feels like punishing players for choosing to pursue some interesting story points.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a real easy question to answer- so someone who would have fun playing a seemingless changeling can do so. <br /> <br /> And it's hardly a great loss being seemingless- so far all we know is that you lose out on an advantage and a disadvantage, and some contract affinity which is no great loss if you aren't planning on buying those contracts anyway. <br /> <br /> Unless something drastic is added to seemings, then being seemingless is a minor disadvantage at best. <br /> <br /> And unless your ST is going to put a gun to your head and force you to play a seemingless changeling I fail to see how an extra option is going to dampen your fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:07:25-07:00","id":505807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=505166#post505166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a real easy question to answer- so someone who would have fun playing a seemingless changeling can do so.<br /> <br /> And it's hardly a great loss being seemingless- so far all we know is that you lose out on an advantage and a disadvantage, and some contract affinity which is no great loss if you aren't planning on buying those contracts anyway.<br /> <br /> Unless something drastic is added to seemings, then being seemingless is a minor disadvantage at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you're correct that the absence may feel overstated, I think it is a bigger one than alluded here. From David's remarks, the majority of Contracts will be of the universal variety. The way those work, going by the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Outline</a>,* is that you buy the Contract for 1-5 experiences (depending on its rating). Each universal Contract has one or more favored Seemings (6 is called out as rare), for which it gives an additional or focused benefit: if you're a member of a listed Seeming, you get its version free when you buy the Contract. If you're not, or you want to also buy another Seeming's version, you can pay an experience to learn it from a member of another Seeming. If you have no Seeming, you always have to pay that experience to learn from someone else if you're to get an extra benefit from it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, while it's clear there's a gap, the degree to which this point matters will depend on how good the favored Seeming benefits actually are. If they're more of a nice touch, then it's probably not a significant impediment. If they can make a Contract much more useful, I can see how that could ruffle some feathers.<br /> <br /> That said, with the emphasis on agency, I'll probably actually be okay with having a difference like this. Probably. It'll depend on one very important question to me: if a Changeling clearly reclaims his or her life and agency in a significant way but also really doesn't line up with any of the six Seemings, what happens? Does the character just get the closest Seeming to the manner of escape that will fit (which is less than ideal, but okay), or does she wind up Seeming-less? If it's the latter, I feel like that breaks the metaphor for me: having a Seeming feels less like a manifestation of the agency a character reclaimed, and instead feels like that's true only if the character's reclamation was one of the 6** specific &quot;right&quot; ways to go about it. The achievement isn't diminished for those who manage it, but it would lose a lot of luster for me.<br /> <br /> Of course, that concern also depends on all six Seemings collectively feeling like they leave sizable gaps in ways to reclaim agency that aren't caught by any of them. That's impossible to say without seeing all the write-ups and any lead-in to the Seeming section, but I'd be lying if I said it wasn't a mild concern: the three we've seen feel just a bit too specific to me.<br /> <br /> Hmm... Didn't really intend for that reply to morph into a perhaps poorly written expression of my likely baseless primary source for 2e trepidation, but there we go. ^_^o<br /> <br /> * See the relevant section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2e Outline, on Universal Contracts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These have a single name. They\u2019re lone powers. They have dot ratings, you buy them at their dot rating. So, a three dot contract costs 3 experiences. These each have one or more favored seemings, where they do an additional or focused thing. You could theoretically list six favored seemings. That should be rare. If you have that seeming, you get it for free. Otherwise, you have to find a member of that seeming to teach you, and it costs one experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>** Yes, and eventually 7, possibly 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:20:41-07:00","id":506252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=503592#post503592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Seeming is, is you establishing your own power and independence. So the way I see it, the Changeling could still develop a Seeming based on how they decide to use their new &quot;gifts&quot; once they've been released. Loyalists don't have a Seeming because, well, they're still submissive to their Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div> There was teasing about a seventh seeming. Maybe that one is for loyalists!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:40:42-07:00","id":506268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=505161#post505161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand why the &quot;no seeming&quot; thing even exists as the inevitable result of being willingly let go by the fae. Can someone explain why that's a worthwhile change to the game, or why it's worth subtracting the mechanical advantage/interest of seemings from that plethora of interesting character backstories?<br /> <br /> I know I can come across as overly negative at times - but I'm this one has me scratching my head more than most... and I'm not generally familiar enough with Changeling as it stands to hold an opinion other than my first impression of &quot;this feels like punishing players for choosing to pursue some interesting story points.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No Blessing or Curse hanging over your head. You are not as bound to a story as anyone else, so your choices are more your own, neither benefiting or falling because of certain behaviors.<br /> <br /> It also creates a bit on an interesting situation of social stigma-at the least, you didn't <i>do</i> anything to set yourself free, and at the most, you're very likely a loyalist.On the other hand, you're not as prone as seeing the world in particular ways.<br /> <br /> But mostly, in a game about overcoming and owning scars, there's a lot of interesting questions to be explored about someone who isn't as damaged as the others and how they relate to everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T19:34:03-07:00","id":506341,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't see why being let go after your term of service is done needs to equate to &quot;no seeming.&quot; Maybe your method of retaining agency was in stoically enduring the torments of your Durance, quietly looking forward to the freedom which will be yours, soon. Or maybe you tricked your Keeper into adhering to the terms of a pledge it had intended to loophole out of. Point being, there are plenty of ways that &quot;released by his Keeper&quot; can coincide with &quot;Displayed his own agency&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:04:59-07:00","id":506348,"title":"","content":"Stoic Endurance is not an act of Agency. You don't get a gold (or should that be red?) star for just sitting there. You don't escape barb wires by just sitting there.<br /> <br /> Even if I ignore some of the real world parallels(Which I'm going to, because 'Stoic Endurance' in those circumstances makes me furious), the Wyrd is a narrative force. Protagonists aren't protagonists because they sit there, but because they are <i>pro-active agents</i>. A character who does nothing to handle the conflict and instead idly prays for its' passing isn't going to be rewarded.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't we get pissed at characters who get all the reward when they do nothing for it? Don't we hate heroes who haven't earned their heroism in fiction, the stories that tell us we should praise them just cause? The Wyrd is no different.<br /> <br /> The one who sits, the one who waits, the one who accepts-there is no Path to the Tower of Revolution for that one. And when they escape, they are going to have to come to terms with that, until they develop the adolescence needed to confront their world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-06-2015, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:16:34-07:00","id":506356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501754-second-edition-concept-concern?p=506348#post506348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protagonists aren't protagonists because they sit there, but because they are <i>pro-active agents</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to chime in here with a contrasting but complementary point:<br /> <br /> I took a playwriting course as part of the requirements to get my bachelor's degree. It was rather more of a learning experience for me than other mostly-workshop-based courses I'd taken in the past. Part of that amounts to the fact that we were mostly making ten-page one-acts that we had to run through a worksheet explaining some of our intentions and assessments of our own work.<br /> <br /> The answer to &quot;who is the protagonist in this play?&quot; was supposed to be determined by which character<i> changed through the events of the story.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494854#post494854\">Something changes. Ha.</a>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-06-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:37:54-07:00","id":506363,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna head off the inevitable and ask the question I know the answer to already: How is that complementary? You're basically saying that active decisions aren't needed, just change, which can be inflicted by weathering the trauma, which contradicts what I say.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I'll get to it tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-07-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}